# API Architecture (SoC)

## Layers (one job each)

| Layer | Folder | Allowed to do | Must NOT do |
|---|---|---|---|
| Route handlers | `app/api/**/route.ts` | Parse req, validate, call service, return Response | Business rules, prompt/mock text, keyword lists |
| Services | `lib/server/coach/service.ts` | Orchestration | HTTP `Request`/`Response` details beyond inputs |
| Mock / safety | `lib/server/coach/mock.ts`, `safety.ts` | Deterministic replies + crisis heuristics | Touch HTTP |
| Schema | `lib/server/coach/schema.ts` | Zod request/response only | Side effects |
| Errors | `lib/server/errors.ts` | Typed errors / helpers | Feature orchestration |

## Naming

Folder already states the role: `service.ts`, not `coach.service.ts`.

## No database layer

No repositories/models. Do not invent a fake DB layer.

## No LLM client (current)

Coach is mock-only. Do not add `openai.ts` or provider SDKs until `docs/TECH.md` is updated.
Keep `getCoachReply(input)` as the stable service interface so a provider can replace `mock.ts` later.

## Route handlers stay thin

```ts
// ✅ thin
export async function POST(request: Request) {
  const body = await request.json();
  const input = coachRequestSchema.parse(body);
  const result = await getCoachReply(input);
  return Response.json(result);
}
```
